WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.030
A globe spins, then shrinks, and shrinks,

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.400
until it is one kitchen table.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:08.410
Then it grows back.

4
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:13.020
A thread of light runs out from
it to two texts, nothing alike.

5
00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:17.280
One issue, the whole
world, one kitchen table.

6
00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.690
So what makes an issue global?

7
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.310
And how can two texts share one?

8
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.180
In this mission, you'll learn
what the Individual Oral asks:

9
00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.810
one global issue, explored
through two texts.

10
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.920
You'll put possible issues
through three tests.

11
00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.320
You'll meet the five fields of
inquiry, as starting points.

12
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:40.830
And you'll test whether two texts that
are nothing alike can really share one

13
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:41.770
issue.

14
00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.930
Your mission: explain what
makes an issue global,

15
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.020
and how two texts share it.
